{"name":"Aerodynamic","hex":"#cacecd","fetched":"2026-10-19","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aerodynamic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, or relating to the science of aerodynamics.","Having a shape that reduces drag when moving through the air."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aerodynamic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aerodynamic (instrumental)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Aerodynamic\" is an instrumental track by French duo Daft Punk, featuring a prominent guitar solo. The track was released on 28 March 2001 as the second single from the Discovery album. \"Aerodynamic\" hit the U.S. dance charts through club play as the B-side to \"Digital Love\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d5/DaftPunk_Aerodynamic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aerodynamic_(instrumental)","wikidata":"Q2698216"},{"title":"Aerodynamics","blocks":[{"text":"Aerodynamics is the study of the motion of air, particularly when affected by a solid object, such as an airplane wing. It involves topics covered in the field of fluid dynamics and its subfield of gas dynamics, and is an important domain of study in aeronautics. The term aerodynamics is often used synonymously with gas dynamics, the difference being that \"gas dynamics\" applies to the study of the motion of all gases, and is not limited to air. The formal study of aerodynamics began in the modern sense in the eighteenth century, although observations of fundamental concepts such as aerodynamic drag were recorded much earlier. Most of the early efforts in aerodynamics were directed toward achieving heavier-than-air flight, which was first demonstrated by Otto Lilienthal in 1891. Since then, the use of aerodynamics through mathematical analysis, empirical approximations, wind tunnel experimentation, and computer simulations has formed a rational basis for the development of heavier-than-air flight and a number of other technologies. Recent work in aerodynamics has focused on issues related to compressible flow, turbulence, and boundary layers. Computational aerodynamics is an interdisciplinary field and a specialization of computational fluid dynamics that develops algorithms to solve problems related to aerodynamics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg/330px-Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aerodynamics","wikidata":"Q8424"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d5/DaftPunk_Aerodynamic.jpg/250px-DaftPunk_Aerodynamic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d5/DaftPunk_Aerodynamic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d5/DaftPunk_Aerodynamic.jpg/250px-DaftPunk_Aerodynamic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADaftPunk_Aerodynamic.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg/500px-Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg/1280px-Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg/500px-Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A NASA wake turbulence study at Wallops Island is portrayed, 1990. A vortex is created by passage of an aircraft wing, revealed by smoke. Vortices are one of the many phenomena associated with the study of aerodynamics.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAirplane_vortex_edit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/WB_Wind_Tunnel.jpg/500px-WB_Wind_Tunnel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/WB_Wind_Tunnel.jpg/1280px-WB_Wind_Tunnel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/WB_Wind_Tunnel.jpg/500px-WB_Wind_Tunnel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A replica of the Wright brothers' wind tunnel is on display at the Virginia Air and Space Center in Hampton. Wind tunnels were key in the development and validation of the laws of aerodynamics.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWB_Wind_Tunnel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Smooth_Finish_Makes_Smooth_Flying_Art.IWMPST14268.jpg/330px-Smooth_Finish_Makes_Smooth_Flying_Art.IWMPST14268.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Smooth_Finish_Makes_Smooth_Flying_Art.IWMPST14268.jpg/330px-Smooth_Finish_Makes_Smooth_Flying_Art.IWMPST14268.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Ministry of Aircraft Production poster on aerodynamics","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmooth_Finish_Makes_Smooth_Flying_Art.IWMPST14268.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3840x1080_F16_OpenFOAM.jpg/500px-3840x1080_F16_OpenFOAM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3840x1080_F16_OpenFOAM.jpg/1280px-3840x1080_F16_OpenFOAM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wik